WEBVTT

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:07.230
We will now begin the withdrawal exam for Inazuma Japan.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:11.270
If you pass, I will allow you to withdraw from the team.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.740
Of course, I will also fulfill the terms of your contract.

00:00:15.470 --> 00:00:17.200
Coach... Are you serious?!

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.850
But, can you imagine this?

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:25.770
Once this exam is over, not one of you will desire to leave this team.

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:31.150
What does he mean?

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:32.340
I don't know.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:16.920
What is Coach thinking?

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:20.470
It just sounds to me that he's okay with us quitting.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.930
The exam will consist of a PK match.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:27.620
PK match?

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.300
It's when you face the goalkeeper one-on-one to make a goal.

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.630
Sounds easy enough.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.550
You will be given five chances to shoot.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:40.020
Miss all of them, and you pass the exam.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:44.380
Coach! Don't you mean, if we <i>make in</i>  all of them?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:45.640
You heard me.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:48.770
We're not supposed to score a goal, but miss?

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.480
What a strange exam.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.400
Who will be goalkeeper?

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:54.620
There is no need for one.

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:58.120
A penalty kick match without a goalkeeper?

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:01.100
What? That's way too easy.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.630
It would be almost impossible to fail.

00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:05.970
Do you think it easy?

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:07.780
Isn't it?

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.870
Let me inform you all of one thing before we proceed.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:21.930
If you are unable to pass this apparently easy exam, you must undergo standard training for Inazuma Japan.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:28.100
Of course, those who wish to stay in Inazuma Japan do not need to take the exam.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:31.060
Think for yourselves and act accordingly.

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:36.050
The exam will be held 30 minutes from now, at Seaside Stadium.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:36.800
That is all.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:42.100
If we miss making shoots into an unguarded goal, we pass...

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:45.320
He's telling the people who want to quit to go ahead, I'm sure of it.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.600
The contents of the exam are highly illogical.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.950
How delightfully interesting.

00:03:49.950 --> 00:03:52.830
That coach really does know how to surprise me.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:56.950
Not that it wasn't within the range of my predictions, of course.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.840
Um...

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:06.570
Maybe Coach got sick of us, so...

00:04:06.570 --> 00:04:10.350
He's telling us indirectly to leave the team, is that what you're saying?

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.250
Yes...

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:12.100
Cut the crap!

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.850
He gathers us together and then tosses us out?

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.070
I won't accept that!

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:25.230
Wait! The coach must have something in mind, so-

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:25.610
No.

00:04:26.150 --> 00:04:29.030
This is a good opportunity for the team.

00:04:29.480 --> 00:04:32.580
You guys didn't come here for soccer.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.530
Inazuma Japan doesn't need members like you.

00:04:35.850 --> 00:04:38.550
Take the exam and then get out of here.

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.630
Shindou-san.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:52.850
If we all work hard at training and face soccer head-on, I'm sure that everyone will see how fun soccer is too!

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.140
I'm taking the exam.

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:56.570
Tetsukado...

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.630
I'm fine with being tossed out.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:03.080
I'll get to buy a ship out of it.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:05.110
It's like a dream come true.

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:09.030
Like you said, I have no interest in soccer...

00:05:10.300 --> 00:05:12.770
...or any sport, for that matter.

00:05:12.770 --> 00:05:15.250
You'll be happier without me around, wouldn't you?

00:05:19.220 --> 00:05:23.840
I've heard that you want to replace your father's fishing boat after he lost his old one in a storm.

00:05:24.230 --> 00:05:28.260
Do you think that by fulfilling that wish, you'll make yourself feel better?

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:30.070
Tetsukado!

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:33.550
You've been chosen as a representative.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.880
Let's aim for best in the world together.

00:05:35.880 --> 00:05:38.330
We won the match against Korea as a team, didn't we?

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:42.110
I don't have time to play ballkicking with you guys!

00:05:42.720 --> 00:05:44.610
You can use anyone out there as a better replacement.

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:48.570
Go with them to be best in the world or whatever.

00:05:48.570 --> 00:05:49.750
But...

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.800
I'll take the exam as well.

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:57.200
If it will fulfill my contract, I have no reason to stay here.

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.600
Manabe...

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:01.580
You do make a point.

00:06:02.130 --> 00:06:05.260
In that case, Captain, I'm taking the exam too.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:06.670
Same.

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:14.180
Sorry, but all this soccer and world tournament business just isn't me.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:16.230
I will, too.

00:06:16.580 --> 00:06:20.750
I got a glimpse of what fun soccer is through you, Captain...

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:22.720
But I'm really sorry.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:25.900
I want to flourish in rhythmic gymnastics!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:27.600
Not you too...

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:29.300
I'm staying.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.280
Ibuki!

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:35.570
I don't care about soccer, but I won't stand for leaving here underestimated.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.750
I'll stay, too.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.500
My brothers are happy that I'm here, and I want to try working at it a little more.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:44.250
Thank goodness.

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:47.000
You'll stay too, right?

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.780
I...

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.510
I'll take the exam, too.

00:06:54.080 --> 00:06:55.220
Konoha-chan.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:59.130
I'm no use to anybody.

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:04.150
At this rate, the team will...

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:08.650
Coach, I cannot read what you are thinking.

00:07:09.480 --> 00:07:13.160
Inazuma Japan will be unable to play in matches as a result.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:16.130
Be silent and watch.

00:07:17.550 --> 00:07:19.300
It appears that they're ready.

00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.250
This is...

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:36.140
How...

00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.800
How do I get everyone to stay?

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.580
Leave them.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:48.080
They were forced into playing soccer because they were bound by contract.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:51.700
The fact that even two stuck around is what I'm most surprised about.

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:52.700
But...

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:55.850
I think Tsurugi-kun is right.

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:57.280
Matatagi.

00:07:57.830 --> 00:08:03.710
I understand you're thinking hard about what's best for the team, but there are boundaries that some people don't want others to cross.

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:05.900
Just leave them alone.

00:08:06.350 --> 00:08:07.590
But I...

00:08:08.430 --> 00:08:10.460
You probably wouldn't understand, Captain.

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:15.200
But maybe ignorance is bliss.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.330
What do you mean?

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.930
It's almost time. We should go.

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:20.370
Okay...

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.470
Stop, thief!

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:34.700
Hold it!

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.200
Damn you!

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.540
You unconsciously protect your right hand.

00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.300
I heard about your injury from Manabe-kun.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.380
Shut up!

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:52.250
Did I upset you?

00:08:52.250 --> 00:08:54.170
I don't want to talk about it.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.890
I want to ask you this one last time.

00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:02.970
Is this really what you want?

00:09:05.900 --> 00:09:07.680
You won't regret it?

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.800
Nope.

00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:13.220
Soccer means nothing to me.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.580
Come play with us, you two!

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:28.070
I can't play soccer!

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.000
I'm sorry.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.260
It must be tough being Captain.

00:09:39.550 --> 00:09:41.930
After this, we'll be home free.

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.550
Let's get this over with.

00:09:46.630 --> 00:09:48.440
Something doesn't sound right.

00:09:59.470 --> 00:10:02.500
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.670
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:30.800
What's this?

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:32.400
Why are there spectators here?

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.450
There are even TV cameras rolling...

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:35.730
What's going on?

00:10:39.900 --> 00:10:41.400
Shindou-san!

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.620
What is this?

00:10:42.620 --> 00:10:45.950
Coach Kuroiwa was the one who assembled these spectators and news reporters.

00:10:46.700 --> 00:10:49.520
He wants to showcase to them Inazuma Japan's present condition.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:53.020
I guess winning the Korea match left an impression.

00:10:55.220 --> 00:10:56.170
This way.

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.050
Let's go!

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:10.060
Here, on this special occasion, I would like all of you to observe the magnificent shoots of Inazuma Japan's elite.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:19.200
Of course, it is only a light warm up, but please use this as the opportunity to remember these players' faces.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:25.800
And then, in the times that lay ahead, please remember how they looked to you at this very moment.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:29.580
They are, after all, the pride of Japan!

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:40.590
Coach... I don't know what it is you're up to, but I'm on to you.

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.050
I see. So that's it.

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:44.550
What's it?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:52.050
He means that there is no way we can miss an open goal PK match in front of such a huge audience.

00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:56.770
This is a particularly fatal blow for you, Nozaki-san, since you're aiming for the Olympics.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:01.270
If you show yourself failing here, it will be a spot on your career.

00:12:01.500 --> 00:12:05.280
Then... this is what the coach had in mind all along...?

00:12:06.270 --> 00:12:09.900
First contender, please move up.

00:12:11.070 --> 00:12:12.300
I'll do it.

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:17.650
I've got nothing to lose.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:20.870
Too bad, Coach.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:23.180
I'm going to pass this exam!

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:27.020
First up is defender Tetsukado Shin.

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.120
You can do it!

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.180
Go!

00:12:37.700 --> 00:12:41.350
There's a 99.9% chance that he will miss.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:42.820
Do you really think so?

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:52.500
He missed.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:56.500
Tetsukado!

00:12:56.970 --> 00:12:58.460
That's it. Keep going.

00:13:00.520 --> 00:13:02.090
If they want to laugh, go ahead.

00:13:04.250 --> 00:13:06.510
I don't belong here...

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:09.680
...but at the sea!

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:17.690
I'm going out to the sea with my dad!

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:22.530
What the heck?

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:26.870
He looks like he's in a lot of pain...

00:13:26.870 --> 00:13:27.950
Tetsukado...

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.370
I don't care about the eyes of the audience.

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:41.460
He missed again.

00:13:43.620 --> 00:13:46.470
I have to do this too...

00:13:46.850 --> 00:13:48.550
This is pretty rough...

00:13:49.220 --> 00:13:50.300
Tetsukado...

00:13:53.850 --> 00:13:57.750
What is there for him to gain by displaying this to the public?

00:13:57.750 --> 00:14:01.110
It's the coach who will end up having to answer for it...

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.850
Tetsukado... why...?

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:07.500
But he's got a pretty powerful kick.

00:14:13.650 --> 00:14:15.020
Tetsukado!

00:14:15.020 --> 00:14:17.080
What happened to that drive of yours in the Korea match?!

00:14:23.570 --> 00:14:25.020
Those eyes...

00:14:25.370 --> 00:14:27.010
I've seen them before.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.850
Shin! If all you're gonna do is run, then get out of the ring!

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.310
I don't see those legs moving!

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:42.690
What's the point in running? Attack!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:46.150
Punch him! Punch him out!

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:47.500
Damn it!

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.490
Shin! If all you're gonna do is run, then get out of the ring!

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:59.000
Last shoot.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:05.950
If I miss this, I can buy my dad the boat he wants.

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:08.220
I have no reason to hesitate.

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.720
No reason at all.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:14.100
Everyone's scared of being punched.

00:15:14.470 --> 00:15:17.770
But if you run from it, then you can't say you've fought it.

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:23.770
If you're a man, then stand up to the punches without running away.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:25.950
I guarantee you that's a better feeling.

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:27.270
Tetsu-san...

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:32.280
So, I hear you yelled at your dad saying you'd buy his boat for him.

00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:34.850
He looked happy when he told me that.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:40.820
If you're a man, then stand up to the punches without running away, huh...

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:42.870
Tetsukado!

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:45.520
You were cool in the Korea match!

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.920
Remember that match!

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:58.500
Yeah, that did feel good.

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:02.940
<i>Is this really what you want?</i>

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:22.800
Sorry, Dad...

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:26.520
You'll have to wait for me some more before we can go fishing together.

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.700
Tetsukado!

00:16:28.950 --> 00:16:30.270
It went in!

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:37.760
Nice shoot.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.020
Good job, Tetsukado!

00:16:41.300 --> 00:16:42.770
What happened?

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.400
Did you give in to the pressure of the supporters?

00:16:46.050 --> 00:16:47.940
Yeah, you could say that.

00:16:50.850 --> 00:16:54.220
This is the power of those who watch over you.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:56.610
Next up, please.

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.100
'Kay.

00:16:58.470 --> 00:17:01.700
Our second contender is midfielder Kusaka Ryuuji.

00:17:01.970 --> 00:17:03.200
You can do it, Kusaka!

00:17:08.330 --> 00:17:10.670
Fighting shoot, Kusaka-style!

00:17:12.300 --> 00:17:13.150
That's it!

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:14.010
So cool!

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.220
You too?

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:19.470
You'll understand once you stand there for yourselves.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.770
It ticks me off how it feels like we played right into the coach's hands, though.

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:29.270
Our third contender is defender Manabe Jin'ichirou.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.200
All right!

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:46.040
He seemed kind of snippy about it...

00:17:46.650 --> 00:17:50.570
Our fourth contender is defender Minaho Kazuto.

00:17:58.900 --> 00:18:02.720
Our fifth contender is midfielder Nozaki Sakura.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.270
Oh, what a pain.

00:18:19.870 --> 00:18:21.700
This sucks.

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.420
Thank you, Tetsukado!

00:18:23.420 --> 00:18:27.150
You making the goal motivated everyone else to join you!

00:18:27.150 --> 00:18:28.950
Wha... It was nothing like that!

00:18:30.220 --> 00:18:36.320
Now that I can't buy my dad his boat through boxing, I'll just have to make that dream come true through soccer.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.420
That's all!

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:38.970
Tetsukado.

00:18:39.770 --> 00:18:44.510
Damn, you made me remember what Tetsu-san once told me.

00:18:44.900 --> 00:18:46.050
Tetsu-san?

00:18:46.820 --> 00:18:49.390
He's my mentor in boxing.

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:54.370
Our sixth contender is defender Morimura Konoha.

00:18:56.500 --> 00:18:57.740
I have to miss.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:12.450
Morimura! You can do it!

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:13.750
Take it slow!

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.920
Aw, she missed.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.200
No, don't go that way!

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:36.480
Whoa...

00:19:40.770 --> 00:19:41.950
You did it, Konoha-chan!

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:45.160
It went in...

00:19:47.000 --> 00:19:49.700
This is the power of supportive words...

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:53.370
From supporters and friends alike.

00:19:55.400 --> 00:19:58.500
Did you enjoy our little spectacle, everyone?

00:19:59.200 --> 00:20:01.450
They still have much room for improvement...

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:08.350
...but surely, they will not forget the sincere support you have shown us today, and will work to improve themselves every day.

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:14.150
The support of our fans gives our members absolute strength.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:17.770
Please continue to support Inazuma Japan from now on.

00:20:21.370 --> 00:20:26.420
Well, since it is a rare event, perhaps by continuing with it a little more I will find it interesting.

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:31.750
Also, having experience as Japan's representative may come in handy in the future.

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.120
Manabe-kun, Minaho-kun. We're not done yet.

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:50.250
This training menu is too hard for me!

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:52.150
It isn't rational at all.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:59.610
You promised Coach that if you didn't pass the withdrawal exam, you'd go through with standard training, remember?

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:01.770
Yes, but...

00:21:01.770 --> 00:21:04.860
If I knew it would be like this, maybe I should have quit after all.

00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.870
Let's do our best, Captain.

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:11.520
Tetsukado...

00:21:14.470 --> 00:21:16.650
We're going to do running dribbling drills next.

00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:22.000
I need at least 30 more minutes to recover.

00:21:22.000 --> 00:21:23.920
That's too long for a break.

00:21:24.820 --> 00:21:27.320
You there! Train seriously!

00:22:54.150 --> 00:22:58.450
Our second match is against Australia's Big Waves!

00:22:58.450 --> 00:23:00.900
Sakura's plays stir up trouble!

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:03.350
Next, The Enemy Within The Team!

00:23:03.350 --> 00:23:05.190
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.170 --> 00:23:19.620
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:23.200 --> 00:23:26.670
If you're a man, then stand up to the punches without running away!

00:23:26.670 --> 00:23:27.850
That's all!
